rces  it will be extremely dangerous for jews  in france  the left-leaning french government seems  to have underestimated the explosive  situation  alternately advocating toughness and  de-escalation  but that has been ineffectual against  anti-semitic writing  most of the demonstrators came to  sarcelle from other areas of paris  police were unprepared  that has led to an official call for the  town to have its own security zone  there is fear that the unique  multicultural life of the municipality  will be lost  the biggest group immigrated to saucell  in the 1960s when algeria gained  independence and they had to leave  there was a great deal of building to  accommodate them  as a result there are many jews as well  as muslims from the  despite their common roots the offensive  in gaza has divided the people here  the jews are concerned about their  relatives in israel  the muslims feel solidarity with the  palestinians in the gaza strip  like everybody else is  it's just too much  they're civilians women and children are  being killed it's not possible i've  never seen anything like it  the jewish community fears the next wave  of attacks the synagogue is effectively  barricaded  we only get in accompanied by author  marek alter who delivered the letter  from the muslim clerics  i think that they're sincere and that  they share our opinions but  unfortunately that isn't enough in the  current situation  they're too few that's the problem  normally there should be a big  demonstration of all muslims against  extremism but that's not happening  even moderate muslims face criticism for  doing too little to stop the violence in  society  but the muslim community also sees  itself as victimized  we can't go out onto the streets alone  anymore  people point the finger at us with this  old cliche they're the ones who  destroyed everything here  who did this in sarcelle what's this  about sarcelle we're all born in  sarcello  but the mood in cercel and throughout  the 